# An HTML import's placeholder shows its Alt Text (#1898): a sized
# `<img>` whose src gives nothing (here a `cid:` src, which a page opened
# from disk never resolves) imports as a placeholder picture, a grey box
# whose `wp:docPr descr` is the `alt`, and the view draws that text inside
# its frame, dim, wrapped and clipped. A picture that loads draws none.
# `doc`'s `flow.pictures.N.alt` is the text the last frame drew in that
# picture, else null. The read follows a `shot`, which waits for the frame.

test issue 1898 a placeholder picture shows its alt text
  open copy:../fixtures/html-image-alt.html
  call window-size {"w":1100,"h":800}
  shot window
  call doc {}
  assert reply.flow.pictures.0.width is 200
  assert reply.flow.pictures.0.alt is Company logo
  assert reply.flow.pictures.1.width is 120
  assert reply.flow.pictures.1.alt is null
